#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188003 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188296 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7447ccfe-83a7-59d4-8386-c74a3ab47b89" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Expected Value of a Continuous Random Variable From a Joint Distribution"}] :question/id #uuid "f32f96bc-b02a-54fe-b370-8a384c6ae67e" :question/math-academy-id "e-10102" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n${\\frac{4}{x^{3}y^{3}},\\begin{vmatrix}x \\ge 1, y \\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$.\n\nFind the expected value of $Y$." :question/worked-solution "The marginal density function for $Y$ when\n\n$$\ny \\geq 1\n$$\n\nis\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{Y}(y) &= \\int_{1}^{∞}\\frac{4}{x^{3}y^{3}}dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{4}{y^{3}}lim_(b → ∞)\\int_{1}^{b}\\frac{1}{x^{3}}dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{4}{y^{3}}lim_(b → ∞)[- \\frac{1}{2x^{2}}]_{1}^{b} \\\\\n&= \\frac{4}{y^{3}}lim_(b → ∞)(\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{1}{2b^{2}}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{4}{y^{3}}(\\frac{1}{2} - 0) \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{y^{3}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for $f_Y(y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\frac{2}{y^{3}},\\begin{vmatrix}y \\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise\n$$\n\nFinally, the expected value of $Y$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE[Y] &= \\int_{- ∞}^{∞}y \\cdot f_{Y}(y)dy \\\\\n&= \\int_{1}^{∞}y \\cdot \\frac{2}{y^{3}}dy \\\\\n&= 2lim_(b → ∞)\\int_{1}^{b}\\frac{1}{y^{2}}dy \\\\\n&= 2lim_(b → ∞)[- \\frac{1}{y}]_{1}^{b} \\\\\n&= 2lim_(b → ∞)(1 - \\frac{1}{b}) \\\\\n&= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188211 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188276 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1892c89c-8343-57ff-8c7e-e6edb35bb7c6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Expected Value of a Discrete Random Variable From a Joint Distribution"}] :question/id #uuid "136ceff6-b85b-5686-a69b-5d39ff70d3dd" :question/math-academy-id "e-9191" :question/problem "Given the joint probability distribution for two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ below, find $\\textrm{E}[4X-3Y]$.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=5$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $X=-1$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=5$ | $f_X$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $X=-1$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.35$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.35$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ |\n| $f_Y$ | $0.3$ | $0.2$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore, the probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y$ are given by the following tables:\n\n| $x$$-1$$2$$4$$f_X(x)$$0.35$$0.35$$0.3$ |  | $y$$0$$1$$3$$5$$f_Y(y)$$0.3$$0.2$$0.2$$0.3$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n\nNow, we can compute the expected values for $X$ and $Y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE[X] &= ∑_(i = 1)^(n)x_{i}f_{X}(x_{i}) \\\\\n&= (-1) \\cdot 0.35 + 2 \\cdot 0.35 + 4 \\cdot 0.3 \\\\\n&=-0.35 + 0.7 + 1.2 \\\\\n&= 1.55\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE[Y] &= ∑_(i = 1)^(n)y_{i}f_{Y}(y_{i}) \\\\\n&= 0 \\cdot 0.3 + 1 \\cdot 0.2 + 3 \\cdot 0.2 + 5 \\cdot 0.3 \\\\\n&= 0 + 0.2 + 0.6 + 1.5 \\\\\n&= 2.3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the properties of expectation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE[4X - 3Y] &= 4E[X] - 3E[Y] \\\\\n&= 4(1.55) - 3(2.3) \\\\\n&= 6.2 - 6.9 \\\\\n&=-0.7\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188537 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188276 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1892c89c-8343-57ff-8c7e-e6edb35bb7c6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Expected Value of a Discrete Random Variable From a Joint Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98bb64f7-641f-59a7-a812-6d77dc3d0d4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186185503} {:answer/id #uuid "a941f419-0d37-591c-995d-8af3a83343be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186185504} {:answer/id #uuid "e90482ed-b3a5-55c1-af51-365cee2dbd66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186185505} {:answer/id #uuid "527c70d1-ccf1-5859-a3e4-1c9cb172ee18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186185506} {:answer/id #uuid "57c5a184-30c4-532e-95e5-184b1d37149f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186185507}] :answer-field/id #uuid "6dbd4740-7ca3-58ee-8130-82cc83c7176b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186185502}] :question/id #uuid "eec76c44-d392-55db-8b1d-f24621c0b38c" :question/math-academy-id "q-110404" :question/problem "Given the joint probability distribution for two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ below, find $E[5X - 2Y]$.\n\n| $f$ | $Y = 0$ | $Y = 1$ | $Y = 2$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $X = 0$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X = 1$ | $0.25$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ |\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}]}
